-- Money is not in this module. Membership test: a witness of ordinary competence could testify to the
-- fact (the day a person began serving), or the text of a Law states it.

§ `Nouns for the expiry of the National-Civic Service Law and section 348(e)`

§§ `The readings: three questions the deposited texts do not decide (SHRUG, Meng 2026-10-08)`

-- Fork C1 (05-Q7). The deposited consolidation of the Civic Service Law was last edited on 2026-04-01 and
-- lists Amendment No. 9 (Sefer HaChukim 5786 p. 470) as its last. Its s 36(a) says the Law stands until
-- 31.8.2026. Whether a LATER Act moved that day is a question the deposited texts cannot answer: no
-- later amendment is deposited. A reading is an argument of the rules, never a field of a case record.
DECLARE `A reading of whether the National-Civic Service Law's expiry was moved after the text we hold` IS ONE OF
    `the expiry stays as the deposited text states it`
    `a later Act moved the expiry to`                    HAS `the new expiry` IS A DATE
    `whether a later Act moved the expiry is declined`

-- Fork C2. "The Law shall stand in force until day X": is X itself a day on which it is in force?
DECLARE `A reading of the expiry day itself` IS ONE OF
    `the Law is in force through the expiry day`
    `the Law ends at the start of the expiry day`
    `the expiry day itself is declined`

-- Fork C3. The temporary text of s 348(e) is labelled, in the consolidation's editors' note, "until the
-- expiry date of the National-Civic Service Law, on 31.8.2026": either it ends with that Law, whenever
-- that is (the date being the editors' gloss), or it ends on the printed date.
DECLARE `A reading of what ends the temporary text of section 348(e)` IS ONE OF
    `the temporary text ends with the Civic Service Law, whenever that is`
    `the temporary text ends on 31.8.2026 whatever happens to the Civic Service Law`
    `what ends the temporary text is declined`

DECLARE `The readings of the expiry of the National-Civic Service Law` HAS
    `for whether the expiry was moved`                    IS A `A reading of whether the National-Civic Service Law's expiry was moved after the text we hold`
    `for the expiry day itself`                           IS A `A reading of the expiry day itself`
    `for what ends the temporary text`                    IS A `A reading of what ends the temporary text of section 348(e)`

§§ `A span of whole months of one tax year`

-- A tax year is a calendar year here (the other rows of the subject take it so). The temporary text
-- speaks of "one who began service" and of a period; a month is a span of one month, a quarter of three,
-- a year of twelve.
DECLARE `A span of whole months of one tax year` HAS
    `the tax year`                                       IS A NUMBER
    `the first month`                                    IS A NUMBER
    `the last month`                                     IS A NUMBER

§§ `When the temporary text of section 348(e) ends`

-- The readings above, put as the days they stand for. "or any later day" stands for a Law whose expiry
-- was moved to a day the deposited texts do not give: the answer to a question about the temporary text
-- never falls as the end moves later, which is what lets a declined reading be checked at the printed day.
DECLARE `The days on which the temporary text of section 348(e) may end` IS ONE OF
    `it ends on`                                         HAS `the day` IS A DATE
    `it ends on the printed day or on a later one`

-- The two ends a question is put at when the reading of what ends the temporary text is declined: the end
-- under "ends with the Civic Service Law" and the end under "ends on 31.8.2026". Where the reading is not
-- declined both are the same.
DECLARE `The ends the temporary text of section 348(e) may have` HAS
    `the first`                                          IS A `The days on which the temporary text of section 348(e) may end`
    `the second`                                         IS A `The days on which the temporary text of section 348(e) may end`

§ `Nouns for section 341 and the Order of 5759-1999`

-- src:3654 | סעיף 341 – שיעורים מופחתים [תיקון: תשנ״ח־7, תשס״ה־6, תשפ״ה־7]
-- Section 341 lets the Minister, with the approval of the Finance Committee of the Knesset, fix reduced rates by
-- order. Whether a given order was so made is a fact the Institute's records and Reshumot hold.
DECLARE `An order under section 341` HAS
    `made by the Minister`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `approved by the Finance Committee of the Knesset`   IS A BOOLEAN

-- Fork O1. The Order's s 1 fixes the amount "for each month in the quarter and for a quarter, as the case may
-- be" by the average wage of the quarter's first month. For a quarter the text gives no multiple of the month.
DECLARE `A reading of the Order's amount for a quarter` IS ONE OF
    `a quarter's amount is three times a month's`
    `a quarter's amount is declined`

-- Which class of insured person the Order's s 1 reaches (s 1 names three; s 4 once made it reach employees
-- for a time).
-- The class itself is row IL-04's `A column of insured persons in Schedule J`, vendored beside this row.

§ `Nouns for section 342(e) and the several-employers regulations of 5757-1997`

-- src:3666 | (ה) השר רשאי לקבוע תנאים, כללים ומועדים בדבר –
-- The regulations are the Minister's exercise of s 342(e). Their facts: what an employee hands his employer,
-- what a wage certificate shows, what a refund request holds.

-- Regulation 3A(d): the wage certificate that lets a secondary employer deduct the difference. "A certificate from each of the
-- employee's employers except the secondary employer, detailing the wage paid in the month immediately before the day it is
-- delivered, and the rate of contributions deducted from it."
DECLARE `A wage certificate under regulation 3A` HAS
    `the day it was delivered`                                         IS A DATE
    `it is from each of the employee's other employers`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `it details the wage paid in the month before the day it was delivered` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it states the rate of contributions deducted`                     IS A BOOLEAN

-- Regulation 3C: the request for a refund, with "a certificate from each of the employee's employers, including details of his
-- monthly wage, the period for which the wage was paid and the sums of contributions deducted from it".
DECLARE `A refund request under regulation 3C` HAS
    `it is on the Institute's form`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `it has a certificate from each of the employee's employers`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `each certificate gives the monthly wage, the period of the wage and the sums deducted` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Fork N1 (regulation 3A(a)): the secondary employer deducts "the difference between the coordinated contributions and the
-- total contributions deducted for that month from the employee's wage paid by each of his other employers". If the other
-- employers have already deducted MORE than the coordinated contributions, the difference is negative and the text does not say.
DECLARE `A reading of a negative difference under regulation 3A(a)` IS ONE OF
    `a negative difference leaves nothing for the secondary employer to deduct`
    `a negative difference is declined`

-- Fork N2 (regulation 7(2)): "the rise of the index" when the later index is BELOW the earlier. Section 362(a)(1) adds the rate of
-- rise and says nothing of a fall.
DECLARE `A reading of a fall in the index under regulation 7(2)` IS ONE OF
    `a fall in the index leaves no addition`
    `a fall in the index reduces the refund by the rate of the fall`
    `a fall in the index is declined`

§ `Nouns for Schedule K1 (the most a clerk may charge an employer who did not register or pay), read through section 369(a)`

-- src:4014 | סעיף 369 – אי־ רישום ואי־ תשלום דמי ביטוח – אחריות המעביד [תיקון: תשע״ז־6, תשפ״ד־3]
-- Section 369(a): the Institute's chief collection clerk may charge an employer who did not register, or did not pay on the payment
-- date, the benefits the Institute paid or will pay for an insured event in the arrears; the most he may charge is Schedule K1
-- column B, by "the period that elapsed from the date fixed for payment of the contributions under s 353 or from the date the employer
-- should have registered under s 379". Three questions the texts leave open, each a switch (SHRUG, Meng 2026-10-08).

-- Fork K1. The period "that elapsed from" the start: to when?
DECLARE `A reading of the period that elapsed under section 369(a)` IS ONE OF
    `the period runs to the day of the insured event`
    `the period runs to the day the arrears were paid or the employer registered`
    `the period that elapsed is declined`

-- Fork K2. Column B limits the charge to "the cash benefits the Institute paid or will pay to the worker"; section 369(a) charges
-- "the cash benefits ... and the money value of the benefits in kind". Does the limit count the benefits in kind?
DECLARE `A reading of the benefits limb of Schedule K1 column B` IS ONE OF
    `the limb counts cash benefits only, as Schedule K1 prints`
    `the limb counts cash benefits and the money value of benefits in kind, as section 369(a) does`
    `the benefits limb is declined`

-- Fork K3. Schedule K1 has rows for breaches over 30 days. For a breach of 30 days or less it has no row.
DECLARE `A reading of a breach of 30 days or less in Schedule K1` IS ONE OF
    `no charge may be made for a breach of 30 days or less`
    `a breach of 30 days or less is limited by the benefits limb alone`
    `a breach of 30 days or less is declined`

DECLARE `The readings of Schedule K1` HAS
    `for the period that elapsed`                          IS A `A reading of the period that elapsed under section 369(a)`
    `for the benefits limb`                                IS A `A reading of the benefits limb of Schedule K1 column B`
    `for a breach of 30 days or less`                      IS A `A reading of a breach of 30 days or less in Schedule K1`

-- The facts of an employer's breach. A witness of ordinary competence could testify to each day; the benefits are the
-- Institute's records.
DECLARE `An employer's breach, for Schedule K1` HAS
    `the day the payment was due under section 353, or the day the employer should have registered under section 379` IS A DATE
    `the day of the insured event`                         IS A DATE
    `the day the arrears were paid or the employer registered` IS A DATE
    `the cash benefits the Institute paid or will pay`      IS A NUMBER
    `the money value of the benefits in kind given`         IS A NUMBER

§ `Nouns for sections 28 and 32: the branch accounts and the Treasury's allocation`

-- src:448 | סעיף 28 – חשבונות ענפי הביטוח [תיקון: תשע״ו־4]
-- Section 28(a) credits a payment of contributions to the branch accounts "in proportion to the contribution rates fixed in Schedule J".
-- The branch type is row IL-04's `A branch of insurance` (vendored beside this row); Schedule J prints maternity twice (its items 1 and 2).
DECLARE `A branch's rate in Schedule J` HAS
    `the branch`                                         IS A `A branch of insurance`
    `the rate`                                           IS A NUMBER

-- Section 28(b): the Institute, with the consent of the Council's Finance Committee, may move an item between branch accounts.
DECLARE `A transfer between two branch accounts` HAS
    `from the account of`                                IS A `A branch of insurance`
    `to the account of`                                  IS A `A branch of insurance`
    `made by the Institute`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `with the consent of the Finance Committee of the Council` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 28(d): the general and common expenses are divided among the accounts by rules the Council recommends after the actuary's
-- opinion, with the Minister's approval.
DECLARE `A rule dividing the general expenses among the branch accounts` HAS
    `recommended by the Council`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `after the opinion of the Institute's actuary`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `approved by the Minister`                           IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 32(a): the Minister may change the Treasury's percentage with the Finance Committee's approval and the Finance Minister's consent.
DECLARE `A change of the Treasury's percentage in section 32(a)` HAS
    `made by the Minister`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `approved by the Finance Committee of the Knesset`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `with the consent of the Minister of Finance`        IS A BOOLEAN

-- Fork S1 (section 32(g)(1)): "the difference between the rate of growth in the population entitled and the rate of growth of the general
-- population" times the pensions paid the year before. If the entitled population grew LESS, the difference, and the product, is negative.
DECLARE `A reading of a negative growth difference in section 32(g)(1)` IS ONE OF
    `a negative product leaves nothing to reimburse`
    `a negative product is taken as it comes`
    `a negative product is declined`

-- Fork S2 (section 32(g)(2)): the ceiling "shall be updated on 1 January of each year by the rate of rise of the index last published before that
-- day compared with the index last published before 1 January of the previous year". If the index fell.
DECLARE `A reading of a fall in the index for the ceiling in section 32(g)(2)` IS ONE OF
    `a fall in the index leaves the ceiling where it was`
    `a fall in the index lowers the ceiling`
    `a fall in the index is declined for the ceiling`

-- Section 32(g)(1): the data of a year, for the reimbursement.
DECLARE `The data for the reimbursement under section 32(g)(1)` HAS
    `the rate of growth of the population entitled to old-age and survivors pensions`   IS A NUMBER
    `the rate of growth of the general population`                                       IS A NUMBER
    `the old-age and survivors pensions paid in the previous year`                       IS A NUMBER
    `the rate of growth of the population entitled to a long-term care pension`          IS A NUMBER
    `the long-term care pensions paid in the previous year`                              IS A NUMBER

§ `Nouns for section 2 (spreading exceptional payments) and Schedule A`

-- src:230 | סעיף 2 – פריסת תשלומים חריגים [תיקון: תשנ״ט־6]
-- Section 2(a): in an "exceptional wage month" the measured wage is corrected: the measured wage of the last month before it, plus 0.5% of
-- it, "and plus compensation that applied in the exceptional wage month". "Compensation" (s 1 "פיצוי") is a payment of cost-of-living
-- addition, of an advance on it, or of a price compensation; "the compensation rate" (s 1 "שיעור הפיצוי") is the rise in wages it causes.
-- The text adds "compensation", not "the compensation rate", and does not say whether the addition is that rate of the earlier month's
-- measured wage or an amount in shekels. The caller reports the compensation in both ways.
DECLARE `The compensation that applied in a month` HAS
    `its rate`                                                         IS A NUMBER
    `its amount in shekels`                                            IS A NUMBER

-- Fork W1 (SHRUG, Meng 2026-10-08).
DECLARE `A reading of the compensation added in section 2(a)` IS ONE OF
    `the compensation is added as its rate of the earlier month's measured wage`
    `the compensation is added as its amount in shekels`
    `how the compensation is added is declined`

§ `Nouns for sections 336, 340, 340A and 343`

-- src:3637 | סעיף 340 – דמי ביטוח נפגעי עבודה ואימהות [תיקון: תשנ״ח, תש״ס־2, תשס״ה־6, תשפ״ה־3]
-- Section 343: the Minister may fix reduced work-injury contributions for an employer he approves, who employs at least 500 employees and is bound
-- by law, a collective agreement or a contract of work to pay wages for the time injury allowance is paid under s 92, the total wages being not
-- less than the injury allowance ("תמורת דמי פגיעה"). The facts of the employer.
DECLARE `An employer's position under section 343` HAS
    `the number of employees`                                          IS A NUMBER
    `bound by law, a collective agreement or a contract to pay wages for the time injury allowance is paid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the total wages the employer pays for that time`                  IS A NUMBER
    `the injury allowance paid for that time`                          IS A NUMBER

§ `Nouns for sections 344 to 347: the income on which contributions are paid`

-- src:3684 | סעיף 344 – חישוב הכנסתו החודשית של עובד [תיקון: תשע״ז־5]
-- Section 344(a)(1): a member of a cooperative kibbutz has as monthly income "the combination of" four figures: (a) the value of the services the kibbutz
-- gives its members, divided by the number of members at the end of the year; (b) consumer-equipment depreciation divided by the members; (c) what an employer
-- would deduct for a provident fund; (d) what an employer would deduct as income tax. The figures are the kibbutz's records.
DECLARE `The figures for the monthly income of a member of a cooperative kibbutz` HAS
    `the cost to the kibbutz of supplying living and other benefits to its members` IS A NUMBER
    `the number of members of the kibbutz at the end of the year`                   IS A NUMBER
    `the depreciation expenses on its assets that do not produce income`           IS A NUMBER
    `what an employer would deduct for a provident fund from the member's work income` IS A NUMBER
    `what an employer would deduct as income tax from the member's work income`    IS A NUMBER

-- Fork D1 (SHRUG, Meng 2026-10-08). The text says "in each of the months of the year" of the housing value, "in the current year" of the provident fund and
-- tax deductions and of the depreciation, and calls the combination the MONTHLY income, without saying whether the figures are the year's (so the monthly
-- income is a twelfth of their sum) or the month's.
DECLARE `A reading of the period of the figures in section 344(a)(1)` IS ONE OF
    `the figures are for the year and the monthly income is a twelfth of their sum`
    `the figures are for the month asked about`
    `the period of the figures is declined`

-- Section 344(b) and (d): the Minister's powers over further classes of payments, and over a kibbutz member's income.
DECLARE `An order extending the income of an employee, under section 344(b)` HAS
    `made by the Minister`                                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `after consulting the Minister of Finance`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `approved by the Labour and Welfare Committee`                     IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 344A(h): the surplus of a renewed kibbutz.
DECLARE `The profits of a renewed kibbutz in a tax year` HAS
    `its taxable income under section 60A(a) of the Income Tax Ordinance` IS A NUMBER
    `the incomes of its members on which contributions were paid`      IS A NUMBER
    `the incomes exempt from contributions under this Law`             IS A NUMBER
    `the part of the surplus actually paid to the members`            IS A NUMBER
    `the number of members of the renewed kibbutz`                     IS A NUMBER

-- Fork D2 (SHRUG). "The surplus" is the taxable income less two sums; if the two sums exceed it, the text does not say.
DECLARE `A reading of a negative surplus of a renewed kibbutz` IS ONE OF
    `a negative surplus is nil`
    `a negative surplus is taken as it is`
    `a negative surplus is declined`

-- Section 345(b)(1): the annual income of another insured person is his assessed income less the contributions and equivalent tax allowed as a deduction
-- (unless the small-business deduction of s 87B applies) and the amount allowed under s 47(b)(1).
DECLARE `An insured person's assessed income for section 345` HAS
    `the income in the final assessment, before any exemption, deduction or credit` IS A NUMBER
    `the contributions and equivalent tax allowed as a deduction under section 47A` IS A NUMBER
    `the small-business deduction of section 87B applies to him`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amount allowed as a deduction under section 47(b)(1)`         IS A NUMBER

-- Section 345B: early pension.
DECLARE `A person receiving an early pension` HAS
    `the early pension paid to him in the month`                       IS A NUMBER
    `his other income liable for contributions in the month`           IS A NUMBER
    `he has other income on which contributions are paid`              IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Nouns for sections 349 to 351: income that is not income, and exemptions`

-- The subsections of s 335 that s 351 exempts from, by letter. Row IL-08's s 335 module maps them onto branches.
DECLARE `A subsection of section 335` IS ONE OF
    `335(a)`
    `335(b)`
    `335(c)`
    `335(d)`
    `335(e)`
    `335(f)`
    `335(g)`
    `335(h)`
    `335(i)`

-- Section 349: the Minister may change or replace Schedule K.
DECLARE `An order changing Schedule K` HAS
    `made by the Minister`                                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `after consulting the Minister of Finance`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `approved by the Labour and Welfare Committee`                     IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 350(a): "for the purpose of payment of contributions the following are not regarded as income". A receipt, by the paragraph it falls under.
-- src:3775 | (א) לענין תשלום דמי ביטוח לא יראו כהכנסה –
DECLARE `A receipt, for section 350(a)` IS ONE OF
    `a maternity allowance or a pregnancy-preservation benefit under Chapter 3`
    `an injury allowance under Chapter 5`
    `a benefit under Chapter 8`
    `a benefit under Chapter 12`
    `any other benefit under this Law`
    `a benefit under the Income Support Law`
    `a disability or survivors' compensation under the law of a foreign state` HAS `the Minister approved that law as a compensation law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a compensation under one of the compensation laws of section 350(a)(4)`
    `a payment under section 63Z or 63H of the State Service (Pensions) Law`
    `income taxable under section 125B of the Income Tax Ordinance` HAS `it is income under section 373A` IS A BOOLEAN
    `income taxable under section 125C(b) or (c) of the Income Tax Ordinance`
    `rental income under section 122 of the Income Tax Ordinance`  HAS `the Minister of Finance determined that it is income` IS A BOOLEAN
    `rental income from outside Israel under section 122A of the Income Tax Ordinance` HAS `the Minister of Finance determined that it is income` IS A BOOLEAN
    `other income not from work as an employee or self-employed, exempt from tax by a law` HAS
        `it is income from an early pension under section 345B(a)`     IS A BOOLEAN
        `the Minister of Finance determined that it is income`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `aid to a Holocaust survivor under the first part of section 4(a)(4) of the Holocaust Victims' Property Law`
    `any other receipt`

-- Fork L1 (SHRUG, Meng 2026-10-08). Paragraph (7) lists three kinds of income and then, after the last, "except early-pension income ... and except income the Minister of
-- Finance determines". Do the exceptions follow the last kind only (income exempt from tax), or all three?
DECLARE `A reading of the exceptions in section 350(a)(7)` IS ONE OF
    `the exceptions follow the last kind only`
    `the exceptions follow all three kinds`
    `the reach of the exceptions is declined`

-- Section 350A (a temporary provision, 1 January 2026 to 31 December 2035): a new immigrant's exemption.
DECLARE `A new immigrant, for section 350A` HAS
    `the country he immigrated from`                                   IS A STRING
    `the day he was given an immigrant's visa or certificate`          IS A DATE
    `the income under section 2(1) or (2) on which he pays social insurance in that country by its law` IS A NUMBER

-- Section 351: the situation of an insured person.
DECLARE `An insured person's situation for section 351` HAS
    `an old-age pension is due to him`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `he has reached the age section 351(b) names`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `he is a person who is neither an employee nor self-employed`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `he has reached the retirement age and no old-age pension is yet due to him` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a disability pension under Chapter 5 or 9 is due to him`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `a pension for a stable disability is due to him under section 105 or 200` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a pension for an unstable disability fixed for a continuous year at least is due under section 200` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he has other income on which contributions are paid`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `he is a dependant under section 130 unable to support himself, with a dependants' pension paid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he is a dependant under section 247(3) with a survivors' pension or old-age supplement paid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an income support benefit is due to him`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `he is determined missing and has not been found`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `he is an insured woman under Chapter 6 and a housewife or a widow with a pension` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he is an insured woman under Chapter 9 and a housewife or a widow with a pension` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he is an insured woman under Chapter 10 and a housewife or a widow with a pension` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a limb of section 351(k) applies to him`                          IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 351(k)(2a), (2b), (2c): the young, and those who have just finished service. The months are counted to the END of the period asked about:
-- "up to 12 months from the day he immigrated", "a period not exceeding twelve months", "the first two months after the end of the service".
DECLARE `A person who may be exempt under section 351(k)` HAS
    `he is neither an employee nor self-employed`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `his income in the period does not exceed the Schedule K item 3 minimum` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he receives a benefit or compensation named in section 350 other than unemployment benefit for a full month` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he is a disabled person entitled to a Chapter 9 disability pension, in a period beginning on the determining date of section 195` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he immigrated under the Law of Return or holds a permanent or A/5 visa and was given an absorption basket` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the months from the day he immigrated or entered to the end of the period asked about` IS A NUMBER
    `his age in whole years`                                           IS A NUMBER
    `he is a secondary-school student, in vocational training, in a pre-military preparatory programme or a volunteer in a service year` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he began regular service, national service or community volunteering before he was 21` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he is insured under Chapter 11`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the months the exemption will have run by the end of the period asked about` IS A NUMBER
    `he finished regular service other than on a career commitment, serving two thirds of the duty period and not discharged for unfitness with grave misconduct, or was discharged for health or disability` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he finished national-civic service or volunteering, serving two years or ending it by an injury during and because of it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the months from the end of his service to the end of the period asked about` IS A NUMBER
    `the Minister set an exemption for him by rules`                   IS A BOOLEAN

-- Fork L2 (SHRUG, Meng 2026-10-08). Section 350A(a): a new immigrant is one for whom "five years have not yet passed from the day" the visa or certificate
-- was given. Is the fifth anniversary itself a day on which five years have passed?
DECLARE `A reading of the fifth anniversary in section 350A(a)` IS ONE OF
    `five years have passed on the fifth anniversary`
    `five years have not passed until the day after the fifth anniversary`
    `the fifth anniversary is declined`
